<h2>Why do some MCP servers fail in Cursor?</h2>
<p class="answer">Most of the {{ bad.length }} servers that didn't connect need an account, an API key or extra arguments, and our sandbox deliberately has none. That makes them failures in a clean test, not proof they're broken. Add your own key in <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>, then check that server's page for the exact config and the log from our run.</p>
<h3>Didn't connect in our sandbox ({{ bad.length }})</h3>
<p>Most of these need an account, an API key, or extra arguments, which our keyless sandbox doesn't provide. They may work fine once you add yours. Each page has the log.</p>
<ul>{% for s in bad %}<li><a href="/skills/{{ s.slug }}/">{{ s.name }}</a></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
<h2>How do I add an MCP server to Cursor?</h2>
<p class="answer">Add an entry under <code>mcpServers</code> in <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code> (global) or <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code> in your project, with the server's command and arguments, then restart Cursor or reload MCP settings. Every SkillMaxx server page shows the exact config line for Cursor where official docs or our tests support it.</p>
